// AUTO-GENERATED by scripts/build-bible-v205.ts — do not edit by hand.
// Words: Jonathan's canonical commentary txt. Structure: his Notion pages.
import type { V205BookData } from '../types';

export const DATA: V205BookData = {
  book: "Ezekiel",
  display: "Ezekiel",
  chapters: {
    "1": {"chapter":1,"intro":[{"kind":"para","text":"I'm going to be completely transparent about this book right off the bat. I have been dreading entering it. There are certain books (I have learned) that every preacher, teacher, pastor, and minister is afraid of for various reasons. Personally, I believe that the books of scripture that you are fearful of the most tells a lot about the person who is fearful of them. I knew a pastor who was scared of 1, 2, & 3 John. He said they were books that he just could not understand. Honestly, that pastor did not know how to love others and the Lord properly. He had a somewhat warped mentality about who God is to the believer, and only viewed God as a great Judge constantly watching His creations every move to see when they mess up. Ezekiel is going to prove that point very wrong as we read. I believe it's because he didn't understand the books of John that he was not able to show a good Godly love for those that were around and under him."},{"kind":"para","text":"I met a man who told me that he was afraid of Revelation. Perhaps he was afraid of it because of the symbolism. I think Revelation could be taken in the same aspect as many other books of scripture. The central theme being around Jesus Christ. The book, of course, has many symbols, but the message is consistent with the rest of scripture, and they are good warnings (especially as we see many of those prophecies coming true nearly every day. We are certainly inching our way closer and closer to the return of the Lord). I think the fact that he is scared of that book is simply because he does not want to confront the reality of the great torment and tribulation that many people on Earth will be facing. Maybe he's just afraid of getting confused. Who knows?"},{"kind":"para","text":"I knew another pastor who was afraid of the book of Matthew. That one was strange to me. I feel like if you are going to be scared of any book in the Bible, the gospels are the last ones to be scary. I'd be scared of any Old Testament book over a gospel book. But again, I think this is a telling thing. He said he was scared because it was quite confusing (it's the book of what Jesus said). When I got to know this pastor more, I slowly started to realize that he might be scared of the book simply because he doesn't understand what Jesus is saying. That tells me that there is something off with the Holy Spirit in this man's life. I've seen him do some terrible things with his leadership, and it is obvious (to me) that the Holy Spirit is likely detached from him. That's why a book like Matthew is too confusing for him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now we come to this book, and I have been (personally) afraid to get into it. But just because I'm afraid of something doesn't mean I will just back down. It's a part of God's word afterall, and if God wants us to read it, then we should not fear it. I've been studying quite a bit on a topic known as \"spiritual abuse\" and every book, article, and blog I've read all reference Ezekiel. I wish I could say, \"Because I've been studying up on Spiritual Abuse, it has led me to open up Ezekiel from that set of eyes.\" but that is not how I am coming to this. Honestly, this has been one that I have been afraid to face for a long time because every time I've read it, my brain seems to shut off, and I miss the overarching context. A friend of mine has given me the boldness to confront this book, and request his help for the notes I am about to recount here. But while I've been in a spiritual \"slump\" (if you will) I've come to realize that God has put this book aside for me for a reason."},{"kind":"para","text":"My fear of this book was healthy, believe it or not, but not because I didn't understand it. I think my fear for it was healthy because I can relate to it too much. I've been going through a season of healing from past abuse (Physical, Mental, Verbal, and Spiritual) and I've connected a lot of dots (or found a lot of missing pieces) lately to the real dilemma for abuse. I am not going to try and force a message where there isn't one, but I think it's quite important to look at this book from those eyes. Of course, I will be objective, and try and covering every area of this book with multiple viewpoints, but I am likely going to take a close look at what God thinks about the abuse of spiritual authority amongst his own children because that is something that really matters to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"You might say, \"Jonathan, don't try and force your opinion on this matter. Everything else you've written about is very open viewed\" but, honestly, everything else I've written about throughout this commentary has been a direct stab on my own people because that is something we (as readers) seem to miss the point of. Scripture is for OUR benefit, and it should certainly be used like a mirror!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"But be ye doers of the word, and not hearers only, deceiving your own selves. For if any be a hearer of the word, and not a doer, he is like unto a man beholding his natural face in a glass: For he beholdeth himself, and goeth his way, and straightway forgetteth what manner of man he was. But whoso looketh into the perfect law of liberty, and continueth therein, he being not a forgetful hearer, but a doer of the work, this man shall be blessed in his deed.","ref":"James 1:22-25"},{"kind":"para","text":"Over and over again from Genesis to Revelation we see God warning LEADERS of His people to search after Him. They end up losing track of God, and focusing on sin which is how we get to books like this in scripture. Ezekiel is looking to the nations leaders. He will be addressing the terrible sins of leadership (specifically) and how the leaders have turned the hearts of the people against the Lord. They abuse their powers, claim that the Lord is telling them to act this way and do these things, and turn everyone under their leadership against the goodness of God. That's why Ezekiel will be commissioned to shine light on it."},{"kind":"para","text":"God wants to give His people chance after chance, but they seem to always miss the mark because of how easy it is for sin to blind people. That includes us reading today. However, God is also extremely merciful, and that is something I want to do my best to highlight as well as we read. I hope we are able to take this personally to ourselves as leaders, but also find a method of healing from deep wounds that many of our church leadership (and that of any other leadership for that matter) have caused."},{"kind":"para","text":"I might get extremely transparent in this book (not to the point of accusing or naming specific people or things but to the point of helping you see what I've experienced, how I've learned to cope with these things, resources to help others grow and heal, as well as the emotional and mental depths that every type of abuse will get a person to). I'm taking a somewhat psychological approach to this book. Not just to Ezekiel the priest, but also to the psychology of our God and why He does, has done, or will do the things He says in this book. Of course, just like any other book of the Bible, it will always lead to Jesus Christ and His amazing gift of salvation to the world."}],"previously":[],"outline":[],"sections":[{"start":1,"end":3,"title":"Visions of God","entries":[{"start":1,"end":1,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"There's a lot to unpack here."},{"kind":"para","text":"Firstly, we should note that this was during the time of captivity for Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"We get a better time frame in the next verse because there is actually two different captivities that take place for Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"One is the captivity by Assyria (the northern kingdom is taken first)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The other is the captivity by Babylon (the southern kingdom is taken later)."},{"kind":"para","text":"The important part to see in this verse is that WHILE Ezekiel is with the captives by the river of Chebar, the heavens were opened to Ezekiel, and he starts to see visions of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"This likely had to be quite the sight."},{"kind":"para","text":"John has the same testimony in Revelation:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I John, who also am your brother, and companion in tribulation, and in the kingdom and patience of Jesus Christ, was in the isle that is called Patmos, for the word of God, and for the testimony of Jesus Christ. I was in the Spirit on the Lord's day, and heard behind me a great voice, as of a trumpet, Saying, I am Alpha and Omega, the first and the last: and, What thou seest, write in a book, and send it unto the seven churches which are in Asia; unto Ephesus, and unto Smyrna, and unto Pergamos, and unto Thyatira, and unto Sardis, and unto Philadelphia, and unto Laodicea.","ref":"Revelation 1:9-11"},{"kind":"para","text":"In fact, as we read, we might see a lot of very useful and common connections between the prophet Ezekiel and the Apostle John."},{"kind":"para","text":"God seems to speak to both of them in a lot of the same ways."},{"kind":"para","text":"While everyone else was struggling with their current captivity, Ezekiel is stopped dead in his tracks to see quite the vision from the Lord."}]},{"start":2,"end":3,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we have a timeframe."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's during the reign of Jehoiachin, which is the second captivity (that is the captivity from Babylon)."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite the picture because Jerusalem (which is the southern kingdom) was to be the specific keepers of God's future promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"God made many promises to this land for the sake of David (something that can be studied better through 1&2 Samuel."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Ezekiel\" means \"God strengthens.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That's an interesting name during such a powerfully low time in Israels history."},{"kind":"para","text":"There was certainly no strength in the people, leadership, or country of Israel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ezekiel will find strength through this book, but it won't be in anything in this world."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, it will feel a lot of the time like Ezekiel is quite alone in everything."},{"kind":"para","text":"He has the Lord, but no body else will give him any help or encouragement."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Buzi\" means \"My contempt\""},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a very sad name."},{"kind":"para","text":"\"Contempt\" means \"a person that is beneath consideration, worthless, or deserving scorn.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"At the time of Israel's captivity, that is likely how everyone was feeling."},{"kind":"para","text":"The leadership structure of the nation had lost it's way with the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"It had turned it's back on God, and all the people under that leadership followed suit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Except for Ezekiel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ezekiel will have a strong relationship with the Lord, but everyone else will feel like they are under contempt, not under strength."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, I could argue that Ezekiel felt that he was the Lord's contempt as well, but he certainly isn't."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has not given up on His people, even though His people have largely given up on Him."}]}]},{"start":4,"end":14,"title":"Four Faced Creatures","entries":[{"start":4,"end":4,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now, it's just Ezekiel that is seeing this, and it has to be very concerning to him."},{"kind":"para","text":"He's just seen his hometown in ruins, and he likely thinks that it's over for his people, as well as for his freedom."},{"kind":"para","text":"So, this vision comes to him, and he's likely thinking that God is about to pour out utter destruction on them now."},{"kind":"para","text":"Fire, a whirlwind, a great cloud, a large brightness, are all things that are not usually good to the Earth and those that are in the path of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"California has seen it's deal of great fires and whirlwinds recently, and they are certainly not pictures of God's presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, they could largely be viewed as pictures of God's judgement on this state."},{"kind":"para","text":"We have terrible leaders here..."},{"kind":"para","text":"But the prospect of this verse is that God is showing Ezekiel something very fascinating during a very dark moment in his life."},{"kind":"para","text":"A bright light over a dark land."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is likely that the \"north\" in this verse is more like from above, rather than from in front."},{"kind":"para","text":"North overhead, not just north \"direction\"."},{"kind":"para","text":"So everyone else is looking south (down), Ezekiel is called to look north (up)."}]},{"start":5,"end":11,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"To describe these creatures is a very difficult thing."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've seen many illustrations (drawings) on what is trying to be described here, but I think they all fall short."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's the same likeness that we find in Revelation as well:"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And before the throne there was a sea of glass like unto crystal: and in the midst of the throne, and round about the throne, were four beasts full of eyes before and behind. And the first beast was like a lion, and the second beast like a calf, and the third beast had a face as a man, and the fourth beast was like a flying eagle. And the four beasts had each of them six wings about him; and they were full of eyes within: and they rest not day and night, saying, Holy, holy, holy, Lord God Almighty, which was, and is, and is to come.","ref":"Revelation 4:6-8"},{"kind":"para","text":"McGhee puts it best as he writes: \"The four faces remind us of the four Gospels in which Christ is revealed in four aspects: His kingship (Matthew) symbolized here by the lion; His servanthood (Mark) symbolized by the ox; His perfect humanity (Luke) symbolized by the face of a man; and His deity (John) symbolized by the flying eagle.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps that's the best way to look at these creatures."},{"kind":"para","text":"In Revelation I try my best to explain the deepness of these things in a different approach, but I think it's sufficient to say that whatever these creatures look like doesn't matter as much as their purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"The purpose is still a great mystery."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I had to guess, I would assume they only have ONE purpose, and it's equivalent to what humankind's purpose should be."},{"kind":"para","text":"That one purpose is to simply prove the glory of God!"},{"kind":"para","text":"God could have made us into these creatures that have no choice but to simply praise Him alone, but God made us far more unique."},{"kind":"para","text":"We can talk more about that in Revelation."}]},{"start":12,"end":12,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This (as we will see a few others as well) detail is not covered in Revelation."},{"kind":"para","text":"They have four faces, so they don't need to turn."},{"kind":"para","text":"Honestly, if they have one brain (or even four, it doesn't really matter) they are going to have to trust their other faces to make the right moves in the direction they are facing."},{"kind":"para","text":"One face for each direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"If I had a face behind me, why would I turn around to go in a different direction."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'd just start walking backwards."},{"kind":"para","text":"The real point here, however, is WHY (again) they moved in the direction they did."},{"kind":"para","text":"Every face was led by one thing, and that was \"whither the spirit was to go\"."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a powerful message, especially to Ezekiel."},{"kind":"para","text":"The people that Ezekiel has been around for some time now have certainly not been following the spirit of the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"This creature is setting a very important example for all of us."},{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, God could have created us like these creatures with no choice but to follow His Spirit all the time no matter what (like a cat with a laser pointer)."},{"kind":"para","text":"But He didn't, and we have the freedom to stray away from Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Though, Israel is a great example about why it's a bad idea to stop following the Spirit of God."}]},{"start":13,"end":14,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"If I were John (or Ezekiel for that matter here), I would be extremely frightened by these creatures."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't seem to do anything normal."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are moving very fast following wherever the Spirit is leading them to."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Spirit is a fast working Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are not fast working people."},{"kind":"para","text":"We cannot keep up to God's speed."},{"kind":"para","text":"Often, I believe, the Lord is waiting for us."},{"kind":"para","text":"His Spirit is ten steps ahead and we are usually very cautious and concerned about what God is doing and why He's working so fast, and then suddenly... God seems to just stop. Cold."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's paralyzing when God does that, and most of us (when this happens) try to keep going thinking that maybe God wants us to just try on our own, and then we end up failing."},{"kind":"para","text":"If the Spirit stops, we must stop to."},{"kind":"para","text":"We should not go anywhere until the Spirit of God leads us."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the only way we will be like \"lamps\" for the Lord during a time of excruciating darkness."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Ye are the light of the world. A city that is set on an hill cannot be hid. Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel, but on a candlestick; and it giveth light unto all that are in the house. Let your light so shine before men, that they may see your good works, and glorify your Father which is in heaven.","ref":"Matthew 5:14-16"}]}]},{"start":15,"end":21,"title":"Wheels In Wheels","entries":[{"start":15,"end":16,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Okay, the four creatures we just looked at was difficult enough for us to get our heads around, and now Ezekiel is talking about wheels, and wheels within wheels, and wheels in the middle of wheels (and it will just get more confusing as we go on)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Someone likened this aliens."},{"kind":"para","text":"A spaceship of sorts."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm not necessarily seeing that here, but hey, maybe they are right."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either way, there is a lot of wheely cwazy things happening here... Sorry..."},{"kind":"para","text":"The fact is, we are not going to get enough answers from just studying these two verses here, and if you are new to studying scripture, you must understand that context is extremely important, so we must read on!"}]},{"start":17,"end":18,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Now we have rings..."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe the rings talked about here, and the wheels talked about before are two different things."},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps they are made for the same purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't really know."},{"kind":"para","text":"What I do know is that God makes things very carefully."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's a great purpose for what is happening here."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's intelligent design involved here."},{"kind":"para","text":"The Earth, humans, plants, animals, fish, birds... even the stars and clouds are all made with purpose and intrigue design."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might see a lot of this stuff on Earth (like flowers for a small example) and think very little of it."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you are a woman, you probably think about flowers a lot more than men do."},{"kind":"para","text":"Men (I'd venture to say) likely don't think about flowers really at all."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we see flowers, we probably don't think much deeper than the fact that the flowers exist."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, if we were to look deeper at flowers (just flowers alone) we would know that there is quite a bit of depth to them than just looking \"pretty\"."},{"kind":"para","text":"Flowers have purpose:"},{"kind":"para","text":"They help other plants reproduce (allowing for more flowers, bushes, and even trees to grow)."},{"kind":"para","text":"They pollinate to help other plants survive, and the pollen is carried by bee's, butterflies, birds, and bats (which also helps keep them fed for many other purposes)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Some flowers are used for medicine and food."},{"kind":"para","text":"They can be added into teas, and used for remedies for various sicknesses."},{"kind":"para","text":"Add to the fact that they help other plants to grow as well for our own benefits (like fruits and vegetables)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Plus, they are extremely pretty and add a sense of value to whatever scene you are trying to represent (i.e. an event, a gathering, a ceremony, a funeral, etc)."},{"kind":"para","text":"We could go even deeper and talk about the peduncle, receptacle, sepals, petals, anthers, filaments, stigmas, styles, ovaries, ovule, etc."},{"kind":"para","text":"Something as simple and as small as a flower has very interesting intricate and deep design to simply call it an accident or \"evolution.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"Now let's look at whatever is happening with Ezekiel."},{"kind":"para","text":"If something as simple as a \"flower\" has that much depth, one could assume that these creatures have even deeper purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"Yet, God still has deeper purpose for us than even these creatures we are looking at."},{"kind":"para","text":"But to us (as mere humans) these creatures are astounding, confusing, and far too weird to ever be thought of as real."},{"kind":"para","text":"I think our brains are so incapable of understanding what is being seen that we can just easily skip past scripture like this without a second thought because it doesn't seem real."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now think about how Ezekiel feels as he is trying to describe what he has seen."},{"kind":"para","text":"The wings have eyes, the creatures have four faces, they look like they are on fire, they are floating at lightning speeds, and they have rings around them covered in eyes as well..."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is a normal creation for God, yet it's mind boggling to us."},{"kind":"para","text":"There is no depth to God's mind on creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the creator of creation afterall."}]},{"start":19,"end":20,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"According to this, these wheels seem to give these creatures power to continually follow after Gods Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's as if the wheels are like a battery for them to go up or down, and be able to keep up with the Spirit of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"If their design is solemnly to give God glory in every action, and the spirit is the lead to where they are supposed to give glory to God, then the wheels are there to simply help them keep up with Gods glory (I could argue)."},{"kind":"para","text":"When God gives His Spirit to something, He equips that something with the proper tools to keep up and keep still."},{"kind":"para","text":"I'm glad (unlike some spiritual leaders) God equips His creation with the necessary tools to rest in Him, and work in Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's not up to the church, or to a minister to decide how much God is going to use (or not use) an individual."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is only up to the Lord to guide and provide for His people the purpose and direction for His calling."},{"kind":"para","text":"SIDE NOTE: God calls every child of His into ministry. There are many ministries, but the most needful one (according to the redundancy of scripture) is the ministry of rest. It's a neglected ministry for sure. Most churches don't like when their people rest. They preach about the work of God being done at the speed of God, and people either end up burning out or becoming numb to God's Spirit. That is a good proof that some sort of abuse is happening in your church."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Come unto me, all ye that labour and are heavy laden, and I will give you rest. Take my yoke upon you, and learn of me; for I am meek and lowly in heart: and ye shall find rest unto your souls. For my yoke is easy, and my burden is light.","ref":"Matthew 11:28-30"},{"kind":"para","text":"I've used this verse more times than I can count, but it's still very true."},{"kind":"para","text":"Jesus wants us to be a proactive ministers of rest."},{"kind":"para","text":"That means doing what God wants us to do out of a want, not out of a necessity."},{"kind":"para","text":"If we continually try and work ministry for the Lord (no matter how we feel) we are actually hurting the ministry of God, and misusing God's goodness."},{"kind":"para","text":"It causes a system of burden building in the church, rather than a system of burden bearing."}]},{"start":21,"end":21,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The wheels gave the creatures the need and purpose to keep following the Spirit of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are like the heartbeat for these creatures."},{"kind":"para","text":"Our wheel is our hearts."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"A new heart also will I give you, and a new spirit will I put within you: and I will take away the stony heart out of your flesh, and I will give you an heart of flesh. And I will put my spirit within you, and cause you to walk in my statutes, and ye shall keep my judgments, and do them.","ref":"Ezekiel 36:26-27"},{"kind":"para","text":"But that's a spoiler."},{"kind":"para","text":"The point is, God moves these creatures, and these creatures move out of their desire to reveal God's glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are perfect creations in the eyes of God."},{"kind":"para","text":"We are just like them if we serve the same purpose."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not out of a necessity, but out of a desire."}]}]},{"start":22,"end":25,"title":"A Separation","entries":[{"start":22,"end":22,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This is kind of interesting to me."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even with the majesty of these creatures, there seems to be somewhat of a separation between where God is, and where these creatures are."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again, much like us and God."},{"kind":"para","text":"There's a lot of patterns to God's creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"The concept (I believe) is to show that God is still separate from His creation!"},{"kind":"para","text":"That's a good thing, because God's holiness, will, and design (for creation) is not controlled by the createds input (like some shows or jokes tend to portray)."},{"kind":"para","text":"I've heard some people claim the idea (usually in a humorous manner) that angels questioned God's design."},{"kind":"para","text":"One joke I've heard was about Gabriel asking God in regards to His creation of humans."},{"kind":"para","text":"Gabriel says, \"What is this?\" and God said, \"It's called a human.\" \"Oh!\" said Gabriel, \"What are those two round things?\" God said, \"Those are his eyes so they can see my other creations.\" \"What about that thing?\" asked Gabriel. \"Oh, those are their hands, so they can create things just like I did!\" \"And this?\" \"It's a toe, for the furniture\" says God. \"What furniture?\" Gabriel asked. \"Trust me,\" God says, \"it will be hilarious.\""},{"kind":"para","text":"While that joke is just light humor, it actually disagree's with scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"God does not get input for His creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't believe angels even desired to ask \"Why\" God made what He made."},{"kind":"para","text":"They just accepted that God did what was good and right."},{"kind":"para","text":"They weren't in the same space as God when God created."},{"kind":"para","text":"There has been a space for God, and then spaces for the rest of His creation."},{"kind":"para","text":"When the world has finally ended, everything has been made new, and the New Jerusalem is floating over the Earth, God will dwell with His creation once and for all."},{"kind":"para","text":"That will be a great day."},{"kind":"para","text":"Until then, His creation (including these alien angels we are seeing here) are in a separate space from the Lord, fogged by \"firmament\"."}]},{"start":23,"end":24,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"The Almighty (that is God) has a very powerful voice."},{"kind":"para","text":"Rushing waters is a powerful sound."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you've ever seen a waterfall in person, you know how loud it can be."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's voice is likened to that quite a bit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Again this is another thread connected to John's experience as well."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And I heard a voice from heaven, as the voice of many waters, and as the voice of a great thunder: and I heard the voice of harpers harping with their harps:","ref":"Revelation 14:2"},{"kind":"para","text":"The wings of these creatures were just as powerful."},{"kind":"para","text":"Either it was because their wings were just mighty to wave (like wind rushing), or (more likely) because their wings were quite big and drastic (like a dragon)."},{"kind":"para","text":"Whatever the case, there was a lot of noise happening here, and Ezekiel is really trying to paint a picture for his readers."},{"kind":"para","text":"He wants us to be there with him."}]},{"start":25,"end":25,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously we could liken the voice to God."},{"kind":"para","text":"Ezekiel already called the voice of \"the Almighty\" and now he's saying that it's coming from the firmament above their heads."},{"kind":"para","text":"While (perhaps) the presence of the Almighty may not be with the creatures (or with us for that matter), His voice and Spirit are."},{"kind":"para","text":"Take note of this, because it is the same for every one of God's children."},{"kind":"para","text":"We might not be able to physically see God (yet), God still gives us the ability to spiritually be moved."}]}]},{"start":26,"end":28,"title":"God's Glory On The Throne","entries":[{"start":26,"end":26,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"Once again, we have a likeness to John's account."},{"kind":"para","text":"John uses specific types of stones to describe the colors he is seeing."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is not in black and white whenever someone see's His glory."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's always in immense amounts of colors."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And he that sat was to look upon like a jasper and a sardine stone: and there was a rainbow round about the throne, in sight like unto an emerald.","ref":"Revelation 4:3"},{"kind":"para","text":"Perhaps we have nothing on Earth that can display this appropriately, so these polished stones are the best representation of what he see's."},{"kind":"para","text":"Sometimes my own brain is so undone by something that I have a very difficult time articulating what I mean."},{"kind":"para","text":"It makes sense in my own head, but when I try to explain it out loud, it always seems to fall short."},{"kind":"para","text":"I believe that is what God's sovereignty always does to someone who tries to explain it."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing we can say really matches up to the depths of His being."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even explaining the Godhead falls short in our own words."},{"kind":"para","text":"Using an egg is interesting and all, but it doesn't measure up."},{"kind":"para","text":"Even using fire doesn't measure up."},{"kind":"para","text":"I use His name as the standard, and (pardon my semi-blasphemy but I mean well) that doesn't even measure up."},{"kind":"para","text":"Nothing that we can see or know will ever fully explain the complexity and true view of God in Heaven."},{"kind":"para","text":"We will always fall short, no matter how hard we try to explain Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"Obviously, the man that is being spoken about here is probably more attuned to Jesus Christ."},{"kind":"para","text":"The throne is God's throne of course."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's important to understand that God has a throne."},{"kind":"para","text":"During this time of Israel's history (especially) their leaders have done nothing but get them into trouble."},{"kind":"para","text":"Not just physical trouble."},{"kind":"para","text":"They played on the minds, hearts, and spiritual nature of their people, and made them into a curse by justifying great amounts of sin (not limited to murder)."},{"kind":"para","text":"People were even eating their own children..."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the king said unto her, What aileth thee? And she answered, This woman said unto me, Give thy son, that we may eat him to day, and we will eat my son to morrow. So we boiled my son, and did eat him: and I said unto her on the next day, Give thy son, that we may eat him: and she hath hid her son.","ref":"2 Kings 6:28-29"},{"kind":"para","text":"Their leadership made them this way, and spoiled them so far as to make them believe this was normal behavior!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And ye shall eat the flesh of your sons, and the flesh of your daughters shall ye eat.","ref":"Leviticus 26:29"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And thou shalt eat the fruit of thine own body, the flesh of thy sons and of thy daughters, which the LORD thy God hath given thee, in the siege, and in the straitness, wherewith thine enemies shall distress thee:...And toward her young one that cometh out from between her feet, and toward her children which she shall bear: for she shall eat them for want of all things secretly in the siege and straitness, wherewith thine enemy shall distress thee in thy gates.","ref":"Deuteronomy 28:53;57"},{"kind":"para","text":"But God never wanted them to be this way."},{"kind":"para","text":"If everyone had followed after Him rather than their leaders, they would have never been in this mess to begin with."},{"kind":"para","text":"But God warned them, God loved them, and God showed them what to do, and instead they ignored and rejected Him."}]},{"start":27,"end":27,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"This throne (to the world and lost) is a display of fire consuming and destroying."},{"kind":"para","text":"To the one who is saved and set apart, it's a throne of consuming mercy and grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's a picture of power and glory displayed in a leader/Creator of all things good and holy."},{"kind":"para","text":"He sits above even the most profound views of creation, because He IS creation itself."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without Him, there would be nothing."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"All things were made by him; and without him was not any thing made that was made.","ref":"John 1:3"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For the invisible things of him from the creation of the world are clearly seen, being understood by the things that are made, even his eternal power and Godhead; so that they are without excuse:","ref":"Romans 1:20"},{"kind":"para","text":"He literally IS creation, and power, and glory, and majesty."},{"kind":"para","text":"He IS righteousness, and peace, and love, and beauty, and splendor."},{"kind":"para","text":"He IS good, and perfection, and upright, and the law."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the Spirit of eternity."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"God is a Spirit: and they that worship him must worship him in spirit and in truth.","ref":"John 4:24"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the Fire of a soul."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"For our God is a consuming fire.","ref":"Hebrews 12:29"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is the peace that passes all understanding."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"And the peace of God, which passeth all understanding, shall keep your hearts and minds through Christ Jesus.","ref":"Philippians 4:7"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is above all, and through all."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"One God and Father of all, who is above all, and through all, and in you all.","ref":"Ephesians 4:6"},{"kind":"para","text":"He is God!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"I am the LORD, and there is none else, there is no God beside me: I girded thee, though thou hast not known me:","ref":"Isaiah 45:5"},{"kind":"para","text":"What more could one point out and say?"},{"kind":"para","text":"How much more would a man need to be convinced?"},{"kind":"para","text":"It is a great mystery to me that God can display Himself in a way like this, and in the meekness and humility of a servant through Jesus Christ, demonstrating love, compassion, and holiness through His acts by healing and meeting others and yet there are many who still don't believe or turn to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many even in the CHURCH who still ignore the depths of God's character and take the role of leadership upon themselves."},{"kind":"para","text":"They literally rob the place of God in church by making themselves as God."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are saying that they are standing in the place of God for the people."},{"kind":"para","text":"They act like they are Moses, or they are some sort of special creation that knows more than everyone else."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't have the scholarship like many of these pastors."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't have much schooling to hold my own mind and brain into a higher power position."},{"kind":"para","text":"I might not be \"pastor\" material."},{"kind":"para","text":"But there's one thing I have that is far more important to me than these powership positions."},{"kind":"para","text":"God loves me, died for me, and still leads me just as well as a \"called\" minister."},{"kind":"para","text":"I don't need a PhD to know the Lord."},{"kind":"para","text":"I just need my BA."},{"kind":"para","text":"I just need to be Born Again, and God counts me as a scholar."},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Now when they saw the boldness of Peter and John, and perceived that they were unlearned and ignorant men, they marvelled; and they took knowledge of them, that they had been with Jesus.","ref":"Acts 4:13"},{"kind":"para","text":"The greatest need for a man with a role in leadership is only in ONE thing, and it isn't found in dogma or theology."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's only found in the Holy Spirit of God!"},{"kind":"scripture","text":"Rejoice with them that do rejoice, and weep with them that weep.","ref":"Romans 12:15"},{"kind":"para","text":"The reason a leader finds themselves in a position like the Israelites are facing in this book is only because they have detached themselves from the Holy Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"I could argue they never had the Holy Spirit to begin with."},{"kind":"para","text":"They had the understanding of faith, but they cannot grasp the understanding of grace."},{"kind":"para","text":"Without grace, you will not have the Spirit of God to pursue."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you only have faith alone, you will always be working for God's favor, and you will never achieve it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's not how you earn God's presence."},{"kind":"para","text":"There are many eloquent preachers today without the Holy Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"They preach faith is the path to salvation."},{"kind":"para","text":"They are prominent about that."},{"kind":"para","text":"But faith is not enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"You must have Grace through faith for it to be enough."},{"kind":"para","text":"Until you have grace, you will never have the Holy Spirit."},{"kind":"para","text":"Arguably, that is what sets us apart from these creatures mentioned in this chapter."},{"kind":"para","text":"These creatures pursue God's Spirit simply by grace alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"They don't need faith."},{"kind":"para","text":"God has given us the ability to have faith, and He provides His grace through it."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the only way pursuing after His Spirit will be worth it, is if we have the Grace of God."}]},{"start":28,"end":28,"blocks":[{"kind":"para","text":"What a cliffhanger to leave us on."},{"kind":"para","text":"This is quite an astounding display happening right before Ezekiels face."},{"kind":"para","text":"The appearance of a rainbow is something that shows up periodically throughout scripture."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is always there to display God's kept promises."},{"kind":"para","text":"It is no different in this picture either."},{"kind":"para","text":"God is showing Ezekiel that He always keeps His promises before He speaks to Ezekiel."},{"kind":"para","text":"Now He's going to show Ezekiel WHY He's revealed Himself in this way."},{"kind":"para","text":"While Israel weeps and laments their losses, Ezekiel is gaining a lot of beauty and riches from this single vision alone."},{"kind":"para","text":"He is going to gain more once God speaks to Him."},{"kind":"para","text":"That is the only thing God's Word does."},{"kind":"para","text":"It provides more for the reader."},{"kind":"para","text":"God's Word never robs you."},{"kind":"para","text":"It only gifts you."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you go to church and leave feeling robbed and beaten down, the preacher did something wrong."},{"kind":"para","text":"He misused God's Word."},{"kind":"para","text":"If you feel beaten and burdened when you leave any particular place or meeting, it is likely that someone is stealing something from you."},{"kind":"para","text":"That's why it's important to stay in God's Word as much as possible (especially during the darkest times of life)."},{"kind":"para","text":"It's only in His presence and in His Word that will provide for your losses."}]}]}],"stories":[{"start":1,"end":3},{"start":4,"end":14},{"start":15,"end":21},{"start":22,"end":25},{"start":26,"end":28}]},
  },
};
